<div i18n:domain="imio.googleauthenticator"
     xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
     xmlns:i18n="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/i18n">

  <h1 i18n:translate="">Your recovery codes</h1>

  <p class="portalMessage warning" i18n:translate="">
    These codes are shown only this one time and cannot be retrieved again.
    Write them down or store them in a safe place before leaving this page.
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li tal:repeat="code view/issued_recovery_codes">
      <code tal:content="code">RECOVERYCODE0</code>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p i18n:translate="">
    Each code works once, in place of the verification code from your
    authenticator app, if you ever lose access to your device.
  </p>

  <p>
    <!-- UX-01/D-02: "home page" resolves the same way as this package's
         portal actions (profiles/default/actions.xml, three uses of
         globals_view/navigationRootUrl) -- but that name is bound only in
         the CMF action-expression context and main_template's
         global_defines, neither of which this standalone template (no
         metal:use-macro, rendered directly through
         self.recovery_codes_template()) ever gets. Traverse @@plone on
         context instead: same view, same navigationRootUrl method, same
         value, correct inside a subsite -- just spelled in the namespace
         this template actually has. Do not "align" this back to
         globals_view; it raises a TAL NameError here. -->
    <a tal:attributes="href string:${context/@@plone/navigationRootUrl}"
       i18n:translate="">Continue to the home page</a>
  </p>

</div>
